results.highlight:
The present study aims simply to estimate annual rates of increase in output per worker in the main industries and sectors of industrial activity. It is a preliminary step for a much larger study, which should embrace four aspects of the evolution of industrial productivity:

the technical aspect, including technological and organizational changes as well as progress in skills;

the micro-level approach, focused on the Substitution of capital for labour at the level ofthe firm; -such macro elements as the evolution of comparative costs and prices, the distribu¬ tion of returns between capital
